', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nA: 1, Q: 1, J: 1, 10: 1, 9: 1, 8: 2, 7: 1\nValid Moves:\nsingle: RedJoker\npass: []\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Evaluation:\nLet me analyze this critical endgame situation:\n\n**Current Situation:**\n- I have: RedJoker (1 card)\n- Teammate has: 4 cards\n- Landlord has: 4 cards\n- Last play: ♠2 (by teammate)\n- Landlord passed on teammate\'s ♠2\n\n**Key Observations:**\n1. This is endgame - everyone has very few cards left\n2. My teammate just played ♠2 (the second-highest single card, only beaten by jokers)\n3. The Landlord PASSED on the ♠2, which is crucial information\n4. I hold the RedJoker (the highest single card in the game)\n\n**Strategic Analysis:**\n\n**Option 1: Play RedJoker**\n- Wins this trick definitively (nothing can beat it)\n- I empty my hand (win condition for peasants!)\n- Gives control back to teammate for next round\n- Score: This wins the game immediately for the peasants!\n\n**Option 2: Pass**\n- Keep RedJoker for later\n- Teammate wins this trick with ♠2\n- Teammate gets to lead next with 3 cards remaining\n- But this delays my victory\n\n**Critical Insight:**\nSince the Landlord passed on ♠2, my teammate already won this trick. If I pass, my teammate leads next. However, if I play RedJoker NOW, I win the game immediately by emptying my hand! This is the optimal move because:\n- One peasant winning = both peasants win\n- No reason to hold back when I can secure victory now\n- Eliminates any risk of the landlord making a comeback\n\nReason:\nPlaying RedJoker achieves immediate victory for the peasant team. Since I only have 1 card left and it\'s the highest card in the game, playing it guarantees I empty my hand and win the game for both peasants. There\'s no strategic value in passing when I can secure the win right now.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["RedJoker"]}'}
